WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.181
Two rain barrels stand one above the other.

2
00:00:06.181 --> 00:00:08.851
Barrel one drains into barrel two

3
00:00:08.851 --> 00:00:11.826
and barrel two drains onto the garden.

4
00:00:11.826 --> 00:00:14.420
Each drains at rate one per hour.

5
00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:18.458
So the rate of change of x is A times x

6
00:00:18.458 --> 00:00:21.962
with A equal to minus one, zero, one

7
00:00:21.962 --> 00:00:22.976
minus one.

8
00:00:22.976 --> 00:00:27.034
Barrel one starts with four hundred litres

9
00:00:27.034 --> 00:00:28.970
barrel two is empty.

10
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.935
A is triangular

11
00:00:30.935 --> 00:00:34.873
so its eigenvalue is minus one, twice.

12
00:00:34.873 --> 00:00:38.003
As a warp, minus A is a shear.

13
00:00:38.003 --> 00:00:41.133
Only one line stays on itself

14
00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.960
the line through zero, one.

15
00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:48.353
Can eigenvectors alone solve this system?

16
00:00:48.353 --> 00:00:50.030
Pause and think.

17
00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:53.862
No.

18
00:00:53.862 --> 00:00:57.646
Every eigen-solution keeps barrel one empty

19
00:00:57.646 --> 00:01:01.010
so none of them starts from four, zero.

20
00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:04.517
But we can solve one barrel at a time.

21
00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:06.511
Barrel one just drains

22
00:01:06.511 --> 00:01:09.169
x one is four e to the minus t

23
00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:11.080
in hundreds of litres.

24
00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:14.886
Barrel two fills and drains at once

25
00:01:14.886 --> 00:01:18.150
x two is four t e to the minus t.

26
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.030
It is fullest after one hour

27
00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:25.350
with about a hundred and forty seven litres.

28
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.687
That factor t is new.

29
00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:31.660
No mix of eigen-solutions can produce it.

30
00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.317
An eigenvalue can be counted in two ways.

31
00:01:35.392 --> 00:01:38.470
Its algebraic multiplicity counts it as a

32
00:01:38.545 --> 00:01:41.397
root of the characteristic polynomial.

33
00:01:41.472 --> 00:01:43.948
Its geometric multiplicity counts

34
00:01:44.023 --> 00:01:46.200
its independent eigenvectors.

35
00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:49.113
When the second count falls short

36
00:01:49.113 --> 00:01:51.525
the matrix is called defective

37
00:01:51.525 --> 00:01:54.089
too few eigenvectors for a basis

38
00:01:54.089 --> 00:01:56.350
so it cannot be diagonalized.

39
00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.758
For the cascade: algebraic multiplicity two

40
00:02:00.758 --> 00:02:03.340
geometric multiplicity one.

41
00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.049
Here is a look-alike pair, G and H.

42
00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:10.000
They differ in just two entries.

43
00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:14.044
Both have trace six, determinant eight

44
00:02:14.044 --> 00:02:16.885
and a single eigenvalue: two

45
00:02:16.885 --> 00:02:18.590
three times over.

46
00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:22.004
But G minus two I has rank two

47
00:02:22.004 --> 00:02:25.167
and H minus two I has rank one.

48
00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:29.417
So G has only one independent eigenvector

49
00:02:29.417 --> 00:02:30.900
and H has two.

50
00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.089
A tempting rule

51
00:02:33.189 --> 00:02:36.306
a repeated eigenvalue means the

52
00:02:36.407 --> 00:02:39.424
matrix cannot be diagonalized.

53
00:02:39.424 --> 00:02:40.630
Is it true?

54
00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:42.440
Pause and decide.

55
00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:46.698
Not so.

56
00:02:46.795 --> 00:02:49.315
Two times the identity has

57
00:02:49.412 --> 00:02:51.931
the eigenvalue two, twice

58
00:02:51.931 --> 00:02:55.420
and every vector is an eigenvector.

59
00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:58.605
Defective means fewer eigenvectors

60
00:02:58.688 --> 00:03:00.523
than the multiplicity.

61
00:03:00.523 --> 00:03:01.690
Nothing else.

62
00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:06.005
So what fills the missing directions?

63
00:03:06.106 --> 00:03:10.851
A generalized eigenvector is a vector that some

64
00:03:10.952 --> 00:03:14.990
power of A minus lambda I sends to zero.

65
00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:17.055
They come in chains.

66
00:03:17.055 --> 00:03:20.914
The first vector is an ordinary eigenvector

67
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.173
and A minus lambda I sends each later

68
00:03:24.259 --> 00:03:26.660
vector to the one before it.

69
00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.833
So A times each chain vector is

70
00:03:29.924 --> 00:03:32.200
lambda times that vector

71
00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.112
plus the one before.

72
00:03:34.112 --> 00:03:36.388
In the basis of a chain

73
00:03:36.388 --> 00:03:39.120
the matrix is a Jordan block

74
00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.305
lambda on the diagonal

75
00:03:41.305 --> 00:03:43.490
and ones just above it.

76
00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.355
For the barrels

77
00:03:45.355 --> 00:03:49.614
A plus the identity sends one, zero to zero

78
00:03:49.614 --> 00:03:53.873
one, and zero, one to zero: from barrel one

79
00:03:53.873 --> 00:03:56.429
to barrel two, to nothing.

80
00:03:56.429 --> 00:03:57.849
In that basis

81
00:03:57.943 --> 00:04:00.972
A is the Jordan block with minus

82
00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:02.960
one on the diagonal.

83
00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:06.985
For G, the eigenvectors of G minus

84
00:04:07.087 --> 00:04:10.937
two I form a single line, through one

85
00:04:10.937 --> 00:04:12.660
minus one, zero.

86
00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:17.012
Solving G minus two I, times v two

87
00:04:17.012 --> 00:04:21.814
equals v one, gives minus one, zero, one.

88
00:04:21.814 --> 00:04:26.730
Once more, and v three is zero, zero, one.

89
00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.526
With this chain as the columns of M

90
00:04:30.622 --> 00:04:33.589
M inverse G M is a single three

91
00:04:33.684 --> 00:04:37.800
by three Jordan block, with eigenvalue two.

92
00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.909
Collect chains for every eigenvalue

93
00:04:40.982 --> 00:04:44.089
until they form a basis; that always works.

94
00:04:44.161 --> 00:04:47.124
Every square matrix is similar to a block

95
00:04:47.196 --> 00:04:49.581
diagonal matrix of Jordan blocks

96
00:04:49.581 --> 00:04:51.460
unique up to their order.

97
00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.881
A matrix can be diagonalized exactly

98
00:04:54.966 --> 00:04:57.610
when every block is one by one.

99
00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.554
Each chain holds one eigenvector

100
00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.305
so the number of blocks for lambda

101
00:05:03.384 --> 00:05:05.742
is the number of eigenvectors

102
00:05:05.742 --> 00:05:09.200
and their sizes add up to the multiplicity.

103
00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.064
For the sizes, take the ranks of the powers

104
00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:14.667
of A minus lambda I.

105
00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:17.722
Each power shortens every chain by one

106
00:05:17.798 --> 00:05:20.166
so the rank drops by the number

107
00:05:20.242 --> 00:05:22.380
of chains still long enough.

108
00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:26.897
For G, the ranks are three, two, one, zero.

109
00:05:26.897 --> 00:05:30.676
They drop by one each time: one block

110
00:05:30.676 --> 00:05:32.130
of size three.

111
00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:35.727
For H, they are three, one, zero.

112
00:05:35.727 --> 00:05:39.466
A first drop of two means two blocks.

113
00:05:39.564 --> 00:05:42.122
A second drop of one means

114
00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:44.680
one of them has size two.

115
00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:47.782
So G and H are not similar

116
00:05:47.782 --> 00:05:50.023
although their trace

117
00:05:50.023 --> 00:05:53.590
determinant and eigenvalues agree.

118
00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:57.266
A defective matrix has fewer eigenvectors

119
00:05:57.341 --> 00:05:59.002
than its multiplicity.

120
00:05:59.002 --> 00:06:01.117
Jordan chains fill the gap

121
00:06:01.192 --> 00:06:03.382
and in their basis the matrix

122
00:06:03.457 --> 00:06:05.118
becomes Jordan blocks.

123
00:06:05.118 --> 00:06:07.610
You read their sizes from ranks.

124
00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:08.992
Try this

125
00:06:08.992 --> 00:06:13.806
a five by five matrix has one eigenvalue

126
00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:18.048
and A minus lambda I has rank three.

127
00:06:18.048 --> 00:06:21.487
How many blocks does it have?

128
00:06:21.487 --> 00:06:25.040
Next: powers and exponentials.
